# Base URL of the recognition service, without a trailing slash.
#
# This is the one variable that decides whether a build installed on a phone can name anything.
# Unset is a supported state and not a crash: the app runs, tracks and draws outlines, and never
# names a product. `src/engine/liveVision/config.ts` documents that, and the scan screen shows
# the unavailable notice rather than failing silently.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is the only prefix Expo inlines into the client bundle, which is exactly why
# nothing secret may be put here. This holds a public hostname and nothing else. The OpenAI key
# lives in the recognition service's own environment and never reaches the app.
#
# For a phone on the same wifi as this machine, `npm run serve --prefix server` prints the value
# to use, which looks like http://192.168.1.20:4310. See docs/running-on-a-phone.md.
#
# Prefer this machine's Bonjour name over its address: `scutil --get LocalHostName` plus
# `.local`, so http://your-macbook.local:4310. An address here is a DHCP lease or a tethering
# address, and it changes when the laptop moves between wifi and a phone hotspot. The name does
# not, so a build against the name keeps working where a build against an address goes dead and
# needs a full native rebuild to fix.
EXPO_PUBLIC_KART_API_URL=

# Optional. More addresses to try, comma separated, in order, when the one above does not answer.
# The app probes them once at launch and uses the first that responds, so a laptop that moves
# between two networks can be reached from one build. Cover the case Bonjour cannot: some
# networks block mDNS, and a phone hotspot puts the laptop on 192.0.0.2.
EXPO_PUBLIC_KART_API_FALLBACKS=
